==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, since Yatta requires 15 other [[Toons]] to be obtained, try to farm as much Ichor as possible, and try starting by buying Toons that cost less Ichor, such as {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}, {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, and {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}. Over time, you can complete requirements for other Toons by doing multiple runs.
*For the third requirement, have a Distractor Toon bring {{CI|Twisted Yatta|name=true}} to the elevator to you so you can get aggro. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting Research faster because of his Passive Ability. This will be easier Since Twisted Yatta is a {{Type|Common}} Twisted,  so she has a higher chance of appearing on [[Floors]].

==Strategies==
Yatta is an extremely good hybrid [[Toon]], due to her high [[Movement Speed]] and [[Extraction Speed]], along with her low [[Stealth]]. Her Passive [[Ability]], '''Piñata Party''', is useful for both self-sustain and support. What Candy [[Items]] she can drop is based on a probability system; Yatta can drop all Candy Items, excluding {{II|BonBon|name=false}}s. Candies she can drop are {{II|Chocolate|name=false}}, {{II|Gumballs|name=false}}, {{II|Stamina Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Stealth Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Extraction Speed Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Speed Candy|name=false}}, {{II|Jawbreaker|name=false}}, and {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false}}, with a Box o' Chocolates having a 5.88% chance to drop while all other Candy Items each have an 11.76% chance to drop. 2 or 4 Items will drop depending on if she finishes a Machine (2) or gets hit (4), which roughly would mean around 1 Box o' Chocolates every 10 Machines, or around a 20% chance upon getting hit. If you are working on a Machine and see Yatta nearby, consider priming it and letting her finish it to activate her Passive more easily, giving your team access to extra Items.

Due to her horrid [[Stamina]] capacity, saving Items such as Chocolates is rather decent as it can increase her Stamina and Walk Speed for a short time, and other Stamina-related Items, such as Pop, or Bottle o' Pop, are also helpful to accommodate her Stamina. Voting for {{CDI|Well-Paced/Endurance|name=true}} can also help with her low Stamina, raising her total to 120, close to the 2 Star Stamina level of 125. Completing [[Dyle's Floor]] is a priority for Yatta players.

Yatta's Ability works nicely with the Toons mentioned below:
*Having a Yatta in your team with a {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} or {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} can help with the {{II|Tape|name=true}} earning, as she can drop worthless candy for Sprout/Ginger to pick up for extra Tapes, or candy that has use and which grants more Tapes, like Box o' Chocolates or Jawbreakers, helping them heal [[Toons]] faster. Yatta's Items are also a good Tape source for {{CI|Teagan|name=true}} and {{CI|Blot|name=true}}, although they don't need to prioritize Tape gathering as much.
*Pebble and {{CI|Coal|name=true}}'s Item-finding Abilities can help detect the Items Yatta produces much easier, if they land above ground and/or are lodged inside of an object.
*{{CI|Bassie|name=true}} can carry the Items Yatta produces, preventing them from taking up other Toons' inventory slots. This also allows Bassie to distribute them strategically (e.g. Skill Check Candies to those working on Machines, Box o' Chocolates to help distractors or Toons that are slow/have low stamina) to avoid waste.

Because Yatta's Passive frequently generates Items, it's easy for your inventory to fill up quickly. To avoid this, try to dedicate at least one inventory slot to her candy drops. If your inventory is full, consider leaving Items like Speed Candies or Boxes o' Chocolates for slower teammates who can benefit instead.

Yatta can also be good for distracting with her 4{{Star}} Movement Speed and 2 Star Stealth. Although Stamina management is hard, equipping the {{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}/{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}} combo lets you outwalk a little over half of the Twisteds in-game and match 5 Star Movement Speed. However, if it's a serious issue, either get Stamina Items from her Ability or use a Stamina Trinket. She's better suited as a backup distractor in most cases anyway, considering she'd be able to utilize her 5 Star Extraction Speed and Ability more frequently, and the fact other Toons like {{CI|Goob|name=true}} (whose stats are a direct increase for purely distracting) may be more viable for the role.

Yatta is great for solos, with her excellent extraction Stats and mobility. Despite her high speed, her low Stamina can be dangerous if getting chased for a long period of time, especially with fast Twisteds such as {{CI|Twisted Shelly|name=true}} and {{CI|Twisted Toodles|name=true}}. Using {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}} will give her enough Run Speed to get away from Twisteds before losing most of her Stamina, though the capacity makes it used seldomly.

Yatta's Passive can help a lot by providing a consistent source of Tapes from candy, as well as the candy itself providing benefits. However, your inventory could be filled up quite quickly, and even if it's with good drops like Box o' Chocolates, always save space for other useful Items like Bandages/Health Kits, escaping Items, and/or Valves.

If playing with a 2 Star Stealth distractor, Yatta can afford to fill 1 or 2 slots with Stealth Candies, as she's easily able to recover heaps of decent Items to refill the slots with and will continue to generate Stealth Candies over time.

Yatta's Colorful April [[Skin]] is slightly advantageous in a Spring Fever, as its tails can be used to gauge which effect Gumballs or a Jawbreaker have given the player under the color-altered conditions.

